# Keep the build context small, and keep secrets and user data out of images.
#
# backend/.env matters most. The backend image does `COPY backend/ ./`, and on
# the server the production .env is restored into that directory before
# `docker compose build` runs - so without this line the JWT signing key, the
# database password and the mail and SMS credentials are baked into an image
# layer. The container gets them at runtime from env_file instead, which is
# where they belong.
backend/.env
backend/.env.*
!backend/.env.example
.env
.env.*

# Employee uploads and database dumps: real data, and large.
backend/uploads/*
!backend/uploads/.gitkeep
backend/backups/

node_modules
**/node_modules
frontend/dist

.git
.github
.gitignore
*.log
backend/logs/

# Documentation and local tooling, none of which the runtime needs.
User manuals/
*.md
!README.md
.claude/
.gstack/
